{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
 "name": "cdeps_datm_gswp3",
 "description": "Stage-2 implementation of the CDEPS DATM data-atmosphere component for the GSWP3v1 forcing with the CLMNCEP datamode (cdeps1.0.112, fork stage1/EqESM-cesm-cdeps branch instrument/cdeps-dumps): the stream time-interpolation laws of dshr_strdata_advance (streams/dshr_strdata_mod.F90:1292-1391) and the forcing-derivation laws of datm_datamode_clmncep_advance (datm/datm_datamode_clmncep_mod.F90:328-487), with the shared pointwise laws imported from ./cdeps_templates.esm. Three models: (1) Streams - the per-field time interpolation value = flb*lb + fub*ub with the coszen day/night branch (value = 0 at night, i.e. when the true cosz <= 0.001; the dumped factor flb = cosz/tavCosz is then ignored); (2) Clmncep - the datamode transformation from the interpolated stream values to the export state (Sa_* / Faxa_*): tbot units detection and clamp, wind split, qsat-capped specific humidity via the esat polynomials, density, pressure zero-fill, the cam3_5_55 ratio_rvrf shortwave direct/diffuse split, the rain/snow temperature ramp, and the swnet albedo weighting with the Sx_* imports (spval 1e30 = SHR_CONST_SPVAL when absent, as in this case); (3) GSWP3Files - the four data_sources (Solar FSDS, Precip PRECTmms, TPQW TBOT, topo TOPO) read through the esm netcdf reader (metadata.esio_format netcdf; url_templates on the public NCAR CESM inputdata server with {date:%Y-%m} placeholders covering the full 1901-01..2014-12 archive, temporal start/end/file_period matching the server holdings; time axis left at 'all' because record selection is the Provider's, lat/lon fixed 0-based, extent bound to the metaparameter N_REC so index_sets.record = 1..N_REC sizes the shaped parameters). The tests pin the stage-1 instrumentation dumps (stage1/dumps/cdeps/cdeps_strdata_streams.csv, datm_gswp3_streams.csv, datm_gswp3_exports.csv; traced points are the first 16 mesh points of PET 0, all at lat -90, lon 0..37.5 deg, so the coszen rows are all polar-day - the night branch is pinned by a synthetic tuple). The GSWP3Files model itself carries no inline test (its raw-record assertions were dropped so the component loads and tests without live external data; the reader path is exercised downstream by consumers with data access). The 1991-01 file is the one the reference run reads on 2000-01-01 via taxmode=cycle year_align=1991. References: stage1/cesm/components/cdeps (cdeps1.0.112); stream config from the reference case I2000Clm60Sp_f19 Buildconf/datmconf/datm.streams.xml.",
 "tags": [
  "data_models",
  "cdeps",
  "datm",
  "data-atmosphere",
  "expression-templates",
  "cesm",
  "gswp3",
  "forcing"
 ],
 "created": "2026-11-05T00:00:00Z",
 "authors": [
  "EqESM project contributors"
 ],
 "references": [
  {
   "citation": "CESM (Community Earth System Model), ESCOMP/CDEPS: Common Data model EXchange Platform source (cdeps1.0.112) - datm/datm_datamode_clmncep_mod.F90, streams/dshr_strdata_mod.F90, streams/dshr_tinterp_mod.F90, share/shr_precip_mod.F90, share/shr_const_mod.F90 - the reference implementation these components are transcribed from.",
   "url": "https://github.com/ESCOMP/CDEPS"
  },
  {
   "citation": "Kim, H. (2017). Global Soil Wetness Project Phase 3 Atmospheric Boundary Conditions (Experiment 1) [Data set]. Data Integration and Analysis System (DIAS). The GSWP3v1 0.5x0.5 deg, 3-hourly atmospheric forcing (Solar, Precip, TPHWL streams) and the USGS topography the datm consumes.",
   "doi": "10.20783/DIAS.501"
  },
  {
   "citation": "EarthSciModels - the authoritative .esm corpus this component lives in.",
   "url": "https://github.com/EarthSciML/EarthSciModels"
  }
 ]
},
 "metaparameters": {
  "N_REC": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 0,
   "description": "Number of time records the netcdf reader delivers for each data source (bound by the source's extent at test time; 0 so the document validates standalone)."
  },
  "N_TOPO": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 0,
   "description": "Records delivered by the static topo source (1)."
  }
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "record": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_REC"
  },
  "record_topo": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_TOPO"
  }
 },
